    "body": "Three copy-pasteable snippets that build a generator fail before producing any video: two import a name that does not exist, and one calls `from_pretrained` in a way that cannot set the model path.\n\n### 1. `docs/cookbook/diffusion/LongLive/LongLive-2.0.mdx` (Multi-shot section)\n\n```python\nfrom sglang import DiffGenerator\n```\n\n`DiffGenerator` is not exported by the top-level `sglang` package: it is absent from `__all__` in `python/sglang/__init__.py`, and that module defines no `__getattr__`, so the import raises `ImportError`.\n\nIt is exported by `sglang.multimodal_gen` (`__all__ = [\"DiffGenerator\", \"PipelineConfig\", \"SamplingParams\"]`), which is how every other diffusion page imports it (`Kandinsky6.mdx`, `Kandinsky6-SR.mdx`, `progressive_resolution.mdx`, `plugin.mdx`).\n\n### 2. `docs/docs/sglang-diffusion/support_new_models.mdx` (Implement the Pieces, step 1)\n\n```python\nfrom sglang.multimodal_gen.configs.sample.sampling_params import ImageSamplingParams\n```\n\nThere is no `ImageSamplingParams` class. That module defines `SamplingParams`, `SkipSoftmaxParams` and `CacheParams`, and every image pipeline in the tree subclasses `SamplingParams` (`zimage.py`, `qwenimage.py`, `ernie_image.py`, `longcat_image.py`, `ming_image.py`, ...). The same page refers to `SamplingParams` elsewhere.\n\n### 3. `docs/cookbook/diffusion/LongLive/LongLive-2.0.mdx` (same snippet, next line)\n\n```python\ngen = DiffGenerator.from_pretrained(\"Rabinovich/LongLive-2.0-5B-Diffusers\")\n```\n\nThe signature is `from_pretrained(cls, local_mode: bool = True, **kwargs)` (`multimodal_gen/runtime/entrypoints/diffusion_generator.py`). The positional string binds to `local_mode`, so `model_path` is never set and `ServerArgs.from_kwargs()` gets no model. Every other page passes it by keyword (`model_path=...` in `progressive_resolution.mdx`, `Kandinsky6.mdx`, `HY-Nomas.mdx`, `multimodal_gen/README.md`).\n\nThe same two mistakes appear in `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (lines 31-32); corrected there too.\n\n### Change\n\nSnippets now import symbols that exist and pass `model_path=` by keyword. Docs and comments only; no code or test change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41826996812](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41826996812)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41826996865](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41826996865)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41826996656](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41826996656)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
